rem legacy.sys - BR configuration settings that put back pre-upgrade behaviour
rem
rem Each active line below turns a behaviour change made in BR 4.33, 5.0, 5.01 or
rem 5.02 back to what the earlier release did. Copy the lines you need into your
rem brconfig.sys, or pull in the whole file with an INCLUDE line in brconfig.sys
rem (an INCLUDE path is relative to the file that contains it).
rem Remove any line whose new behaviour you want to keep.
rem
rem Source: the release notes in context/dev/tools/
rem   Business_Rules_433_Release_notes.md, BR50 Release_Notes.md,
rem   BR501 Release_Notes.md, BR502 Release_Notes.md
rem
rem ---- BR 4.33 ---------------------------------------------------------------
option 77 on ! ENTER closes a newly opened print preview (4.33 default: ENTER starts a print)
rem
rem ---- BR 5.0 (release notes 1.22, "Legacy options") -------------------------
option 6 on ! COPY replaces an existing file without asking; RENAME refuses one with error 4150 unless -F (5.0 default: both ask Overwrite? y/n/all)
option 8 on ! DIR lists as before 5.0, as if every DIR had -O: 8.3 layout, two-digit years, old meanings of -A -L -N -O -U
option 60 on ! SAVE writes the 4.2/4.3 object format (level 38), loadable by a 4.2/4.3 BR (5.0 default: level 39, refused there with error 2240). Also sets OPTION 74
option 79 3 ! no font errors (6249, 6251, 6253) reported to the program, as before 5.0; still logged. A level: 1 stops 6253, 2 adds 6251, 3 adds 6249
option 81 on ! 4.3.3 print sizing: proportional faces never scaled, fixed-pitch faces stretched to the cell
option 84 0 ! a / in a file name is read only as System/23 (file/directory/drive) (5.0 default 1: tried both ways)
console off ! no console window (5.0 changed the default from OFF to DATA_ONLY, release notes 1.11)
rem
rem ---- BR 5.01 ---------------------------------------------------------------
option 51 on ! new records are added at the end; deleted records are not reused (5.01 default: reuse) - 5.01 notes 1.2
option 22 on ! INDEX and OPEN KFNAME= create Btree indexes, not Btree2 - 5.01 notes 1.6
rem   NOTE: OPTION 22 is reversed between releases. Before 5.01, OPTION 22 ON gave
rem   Btree2; from 5.01 it gives Btree. A configuration shared with an earlier
rem   release means opposite things to each.
rem
rem ---- BR 5.02 ---------------------------------------------------------------
option 85 on ! F1, HELP$ and HELP use the .wbh help file (wbcmd.wbh, CONFIG HELPDFLT, HELP$("topic",1)) instead of br_tree - 5.02 notes 1.3
rem
rem ---- Not activated - read before using ------------------------------------
rem option 33 31
rem   5.01 locks with 64-bit positions (OPTION 33 64) unless set; earlier releases
rem   default to 31. EVERY engine that shares files must use the same OPTION 33,
rem   or they do not see each other's locks. Set it to match the other engines,
rem   not because it is old. (5.01 notes 1.9) This app's brconfig.sys already
rem   says option 33 64, and a later line here would override it.
rem
rem DEBUG AUTH OFF
rem   Restores the old unencrypted, unauthenticated debugger connection so an old
rem   debugger can attach. It is a DEBUG command, a logged security event, and
rem   meant to be temporary. The release notes do not say it may be given in a
rem   configuration file. (5.0 notes 1.2 and the debugger-connection section)
rem
rem ---- Gone: no setting brings these back ------------------------------------
rem OPTION 14 (5.01): two opens of a file in one session now always share a record lock; ignored
rem OPTION 18 (5.01): DAYS always reads extra digits as the century; ignored
rem OPTIONs 1, 4, 7, 11, 16, 19, 28 (5.01): ignored, BR behaves as with each off
rem OPTION 55 (5.0): REFUSED in brconfig.sys - remove it before upgrading
